Preserve `hello --version`: print `hi`.\n- Preserve silent output for unknown arguments or no arguments.\n\n### Steps\n1. **`cli.js`** — Add an `args[0] === \"--version\"` branch printing `require(\"./package.json\").version`. Retain existing `hello` dispatch. Read version dynamically; avoid duplicated constants.\n2. **Verification only** — Run output assertions below. No changes to `package.json`, dependencies, scripts, or docs.\n\n### Risks\n- Global flag matching would change existing behavior; avoid `args.includes(\"--version\")`.\n- Hardcoding `1.0.0` would become stale; use the package field.\n\n### Verification\nRun from repository root:\n```sh\nnode <<'NODE'\nconst assert = require(\"node:assert/strict\");\nconst { execFileSync } = require(\"node:child_process\");\nconst { version } = require(\"./package.json\");\nconst run = (...args) =>\n  execFileSync(process.execPath, [\"cli.js\", ...args], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n\nassert.equal(run(\"--version\"), `${version}\\n`);\nassert.equal(run(\"--version\", \"hello\"), `${version}\\n`);\nassert.equal(run(\"hello\"), \"hi\\n\");\nassert.equal(run(\"hello\", \"--version\"), \"hi\\n\");\nassert.equal(run(), \"\");\nassert.equal(run(\"unknown\"), \"\");\nassert.equal(run(\"unknown\", \"--version\"), \"\");\nconsole.log(\"PASS\");\nNODE\n```","success":true,"status":"completed","index":1},{"workflowKey":"hyperfocus-0","agent":"hyperfocus","runId":"3e4dd028-5180-465a-a65d-391de94a2aa3","output":"Implemented. Seven assertions passed. No parking-lot items. Reviewer gate pending.","success":true,"status":"completed","index":2},{"workflowKey":"literal-0","agent":"literal","runId":"1ba93bbd-85bb-41f5-9a85-84f497afdd82","output":"No findings. `cli.js:3` prints `package.json.version` dynamically. Matches plan; preserves `hello` behavior, silent unknown/no-argument output. No unrelated implementation changes.\n\nSeven reported assertions not independently rerun; execution tool unavailable.\n\nVerdict: APPROVE","success":true